libtmux-easy (0.5.0) noble; urgency=medium

  * Processes(sigterm_timeout=) and start(sigterm_timeout=): seconds SIGTERM
    gets before SIGKILL, per group or per process (default 5, as before).

 -- Spencer Diehl <docdiehl@gmail.com>  Sun, 08 Nov 2026 09:00:00 -0800

libtmux-easy (0.4.0) noble; urgency=medium

  * libtmux_easy.processes.Processes: the process group without pytest
    (testing.Processes is now a subclass), raising ProcessFailure.
  * close() stops every process in parallel; kill_all() for a second Ctrl-C.
  * on_exit(name, status, died) callback; start(env=, sigint_timeout=);
    prefix="" for bare tmux window names.

 -- Spencer Diehl <docdiehl@gmail.com>  Sat, 07 Nov 2026 09:16:10 -0800

libtmux-easy (0.3.0) noble; urgency=medium

  * Various improvements. Better env passing, faster session bringup.
  * pytest integration improvements. API cleanup.

 -- Spencer Diehl <docdiehl@gmail.com> Mon, 02 Nov 2026 21:07:13 -0800

libtmux-easy (0.2.0) noble; urgency=medium

  * New package libtmux-easy-dash: lte-dash, with Textual bundled.
  * lte-session, lte-close, the pytest plugin, output capture and watches,
    env= for sessions, windows and panes, lte-run --tee.

